# Rockafellar Part IV: representation and inequalities

Surface file for R. Tyrrell Rockafellar, *Convex Analysis*, Princeton University Press, 1970,
§§17–22, which the book prints as Part IV.

This module imports the six section modules and adds nothing of its own.

| § | module | subject |
|---|---|---|
| 17 | `Chapter04.Section17` | Carathéodory's theorem |
| 18 | `Chapter04.Section18` | Extreme points and faces of convex sets |
| 19 | `Chapter04.Section19` | Polyhedral convex sets and functions |
| 20 | `Chapter04.Section20` | Some applications of polyhedral convexity |
| 21 | `Chapter04.Section21` | Helly's theorem and systems of inequalities |
| 22 | `Chapter04.Section22` | Linear inequalities |

## Not formalized

65 of Part IV's 70 numbered results are formalized. The five that are not are §22's
elementary-vector development — Lemmas 22.4 and 22.5, Corollary 22.4.1, and Theorems 22.6 and 22.7
— which is combinatorial matroid theory rather than convex analysis.
-/
